WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.780
Pulling up to another day of Tesla's short-time, daily, episode 467, coming to you from Vancouver.

00:00:08.460 --> 00:00:13.820
It's May 9, 2026. Let's get into what's moving in the Tesla world today.

00:00:14.960 --> 00:00:20.980
Tesla Vision now deploys airbags up to 70 milliseconds earlier in unavoidable collisions.

00:00:21.820 --> 00:00:28.740
Tesla's camera-based system can now trigger airbag deployment when it detects that a collision cannot be avoided.

00:00:28.740 --> 00:00:37.520
This earlier activation gives the restraint system's additional time to position properly before the actual impact occurs.

00:00:38.060 --> 00:00:48.180
The approach relies on visual recognition of crash geometry rather than waiting solely for physical contact sensors to register deceleration.

00:00:49.180 --> 00:00:57.880
By acting on what the cameras see in the moments leading up to contact, the vehicle gains a meaningful head start in occupant protection.

00:00:58.520 --> 00:01:08.140
The improvement shows how tightly integrated perception software and hardware can change the timing of safety responses that were once considered fixed.

00:01:09.140 --> 00:01:18.700
From a technology standpoint, this moves critical safety decisions earlier in the sequence and reduces the window during which occupant movement can peak.

00:01:19.380 --> 00:01:27.200
It also reinforces that the same vision stack used for driving assistance is now extending its reach into crash mitigation.

00:01:27.960 --> 00:01:36.800
This capability rests on the assumption that cameras alone can deliver reliable pre-impact data at the speeds and distances that matter most.

00:01:37.800 --> 00:01:45.680
Traditional systems have long depended on radar or contact sensors to confirm an event before deploying restraints.

00:01:46.640 --> 00:01:55.280
Tesla's method instead interprets the visual scene to predict impact geometry and initiates deployment ahead of physical confirmation.

00:01:57.120 --> 00:02:03.280
Filing's indicate this visual trigger can occur up to 70 milliseconds sooner than conventional thresholds.

00:02:03.800 --> 00:02:11.300
That interval directly affects how much crash energy the restraint system can manage before the occupant begins to move forward.

00:02:11.840 --> 00:02:18.720
The shift challenges the industry practice of layering multiple sensor types for redundancy in pre-crash functions.

00:02:18.720 --> 00:02:26.840
It highlights Tesla's choice to invest in software that extracts more performance from existing camera hardware across the fleet.

00:02:27.560 --> 00:02:35.240
Vertical integration of perception code with vehicle structure appears to be the practical route for scaling this timing advantage.

00:02:36.160 --> 00:02:46.420
Turning to a production issue that needs attention, Tesla has recalled certain cyber trucks because of a manufacturing flaw that could allow wheels to detach while driving.

00:02:47.420 --> 00:02:53.480
The recall targets an assembly problem that compromises wheel security under normal operating conditions.

00:02:54.140 --> 00:02:59.960
Owners of the affected vehicles are receiving notices to bring them in for inspection and corrective work.

00:03:00.580 --> 00:03:06.440
Production of the model continues to increase even as these early units receive the necessary fixes.

00:03:07.100 --> 00:03:14.460
The timing matters because the cyber truck is still establishing its track record for everyday reliability with buyers.

00:03:14.460 --> 00:03:21.180
Prompt resolution of the assembly concern will help limit any lasting effect on confidence in the new vehicle.

00:03:21.940 --> 00:03:30.720
One aspect worth noting is that this recall arrives during the ramp up phase when manufacturing processes are still being refined at scale.

00:03:31.480 --> 00:03:39.400
Addressing the wheel detachment risk quickly protects both safety margins and the perception of quality that new models need to build.

00:03:40.700 --> 00:03:51.300
Regulatory filing show Tesla is now ramping its own NMCA 4,680 cells at the Nevada facility specifically for the semi.

00:03:53.380 --> 00:04:00.460
This replaces earlier cells supplied by LG and links cell production more directly to truck assembly operations.

00:04:01.060 --> 00:04:06.080
The change advances the company's vertical integration strategy for the heavy duty program.

00:04:07.080 --> 00:04:14.500
Tying cell output to the same site where trucks are built reduces external dependencies and supports higher volume targets.

00:04:14.980 --> 00:04:21.200
Progress here matters for the sem by because battery supply has been a pacing item in the past.

00:04:21.940 --> 00:04:29.260
In house production at this scale gives Tesla more control over chemistry choices and cost structures for the commercial truck line.

00:04:30.260 --> 00:04:35.940
Tesla is also exploring a system that pulls hot air from the cabin to ease the load on the air conditioning.

00:04:36.380 --> 00:04:44.780
The idea appears in recent patent filings and aims to maintain battery range in hot conditions without reducing passenger comfort.

00:04:45.340 --> 00:04:53.040
By extracting heated air before it forces the climate control to work harder, the approach targets a practical efficiency gain.

00:04:54.040 --> 00:05:02.480
Details remain conceptual at this stage but the focus on thermal management shows continued attention to real world range preservation.

00:05:03.200 --> 00:05:10.920
Shanghai factory output and deliveries rose compared with the same month last year yet came in below March levels.

00:05:12.100 --> 00:05:17.560
The month-to-month dip aligns with normal seasonal patterns and production scheduling at the plant.

00:05:17.560 --> 00:05:23.800
Local demand in China along with export allocations continue to shape the monthly figures.

00:05:24.340 --> 00:05:31.280
The year-over-year increase still points to steady utilization even as the factory adjusts to shifting market conditions.

00:05:31.960 --> 00:05:39.420
The model Y became the first vehicle to complete NHTSA's revised safety evaluation protocol fast.

00:05:40.000 --> 00:05:46.600
The results reflect both the structural design and the performance of sensor systems under the updated criteria.

00:05:46.600 --> 00:05:52.720
Other manufacturers will now face the same revised standard when their vehicles are tested.

00:05:53.220 --> 00:06:00.480
This milestone underscores how integrated hardware and software contribute to meeting stricter safety benchmarks.

00:06:01.400 --> 00:06:09.920
Discussions in the owner community have noted Tesla's overall safety positioning and the way structural and perception features work together.

00:06:09.920 --> 00:06:17.020
Observers continue to point out that these elements differentiate the vehicles in real world outcomes.

00:06:17.960 --> 00:06:25.800
The consistent emphasis on high safety standards through combined hardware and software resonates with many following the updates.

00:06:26.700 --> 00:06:37.700
BYD has indicated it may pursue legal steps after Tesla and other EV makers rejected rumors of coordinated talks with regulators on battery locking practices.

00:06:38.700 --> 00:06:48.020
The companies involved have distanced themselves from the reported discussions, the disagreement centers on competitive practices in the Chinese market.

00:06:49.020 --> 00:06:58.800
Transaction data show used Tesla and other EV values rising alongside higher gasoline prices after developments in the Iran conflict.

00:06:59.620 --> 00:07:06.680
The upward movement in secondary market prices appears across multiple brands as fuel costs increase.

00:07:07.600 --> 00:07:14.220
Higher gas prices seem to be shifting some buyer interest toward electric options even in the used segment.

00:07:15.000 --> 00:07:21.460
Tesla added a max mode to the audio system that creates a more immersive listening experience inside the vehicle.

00:07:21.460 --> 00:07:27.500
The feature uses the existing speaker layout to produce a concert-like environment during drives.

00:07:28.140 --> 00:07:33.340
It is presented as a simple enhancement for passengers using the car's entertainment options.

00:07:34.080 --> 00:07:40.020
Tesla drivers can now access compatible charging stations at some golf course driving ranges.

00:07:40.380 --> 00:07:46.860
The option is being shared in owner communities as a convenient way to combine range time with vehicle charging.

00:07:46.860 --> 00:07:51.460
Locations are being highlighted as practical additions for daily routines.

